# backend_sweep_2026-07-22 — zenravif (zenrav1e) vs svtav1-rs: RD + cross-decoder gate

Harness: examples/encode_backend_sweep.rs at zenavif branch svtav1-rs-backend
(commit after 2ae4d74; pins zenav1-aom 7b972e50, zenav1-svt 3e25f52b,
rav1d-safe 398b0bfa). Box: dev-32gb cloud (16 cores/30GB), load ~3, 8-thread
rayon — encode_ms/decode_ms columns are LOAD-POLLUTED (parallel run), use
only directionally; the committed timing headline runs are separate
(backend_timing_2026-07-22.*).

Grid: 12 CID22-512 validation images x sizes {64,256,512 center-crop/native,
1024 2x2-mosaic (3 mosaics)} x quality 5..=100 step 5 x speeds {2,6,9} x
arms {zenravif-420, zenravif-444 (shipped default), svt-rs-420}. 7018 rows.

Cross-decoder gate: every encoded cell's AV1 payload decoded with BOTH
rav1d-safe and zenav1-aom, planes byte-compared: 7018/7018 identical.

Headline findings:
- svt-rs QP 0 (quality>=~99.3) CORRUPT on every cell (115/115 ssim2 ~ -700,
  both decoders byte-agree on the garbage => encoder-side; boundary probed
  clean at QP 1 / q<=99). Seam now clamps QP>=1 (quality_to_qp_gated) with
  regression test svt_rs_quality_100_does_not_corrupt.
- One additional svt 64x64 q100 cell produced a stream rav1d-safe REJECTED
  ("Failed to decode primary frame"): image 1475938, speeds 2 of 3.
- Matched-ssim2 byte ratio svt-rs vs zenravif-420 (BD-lite, ssim2 30..90,
  log-bytes interp): s2 0.93-0.99x (svt BETTER), s6 0.98-1.07x,
  s9 1.00-1.08x (svt slightly worse, worst at 1024px).
- Parallel-run wall medians (directional): svt ~6x faster at s6, ~4.4x at
  s9, ~0.6-0.86x (slower) at s2 — the linear speed->preset maps do not
  align the two ladders' wall-time.
- Quality->median-ssim2 curves align within ~+-5 ssim2 for q>=35 across
  backends; svt is materially worse below q30 at s6/s9.
